# Stylesheets

## Tokens

- Define color and radius tokens on `:root` and `.dark`, outside any `@layer`.
- Store full `oklch(...)` values on the variable (`--background: oklch(1 0 0)`). Never bare channels (`0 0% 100%`), hex, `rgb()`, or `hsl()`. `.dark` gets its own explicit values.
- Map color tokens in `@theme inline` as plain `var()` with no color-function wrapper: `--color-background: var(--background)`. Radius steps may be `calc(var(--radius) * n)`. A literal `--font-sans` stack is the theme font.
- Name tokens by role so utilities match (`--color-muted-foreground` → `text-muted-foreground`). Never by swatch (`--bright-red`) or palette step (`--zinc-800`).
- Rules consume tokens (`color: var(--foreground)`). No second palette of hex, palette names (`red`, `gray`), or raw palette variables. `transparent` is not a palette color.
- The dark theme sets `color-scheme: dark`.

## @apply

- `@apply` only inside `@layer base` for element defaults (`html`, `body`, `*`, scrollbars).
- Never `@apply` to build component classes (`.btn`, `.card`) or repeated utility bundles. Extract a React component.
- Never `@apply` raw palette utilities. Use token utilities.

## Motion

- Inside `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`, set `animation: none; transition: none` on non-essential motion. A spinner showing in-progress work may stay; comment the exception.
- Never `transition: all`. Name the properties.
